text:
you know, i usually don't often reply, but i am in the same boat in a sense. i dieted (seriously) for 6 months aswell as went to the gym with a personal trainer. i lost 4 stone. i was 23.12 stone and went down to 19.12. then suddenly, my support went (girlfriend) and i went back up recently to 21.08. it's a huge devistation after losing it. here i am sitting at the computer when my work flow is low, browsing reddit. i am dieting sure, but i am not going to the gym, it is so hard to tell myself "don't eat, you are bored or thirsty" but i go to the fridge, grab two sandwiches and pig out, then ask myself why i am not losing weight or have no motivation.

&amp;#x200b;

the tl;dr of this to you is, thanks. reading this has motivated me to get off my ass, apply to the gym and hit it again. heres hoping the motivation and dopamine from the gym days will help me through it, so thank you for helping me finally push the ball up the last bit of the hill i had to climb before i could get it rolling.
